  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Nature and Manifestation
    
    A wild magic that surfaces in fractured ice-zones where aurora-light and geothermal pressure converge. ☽'zenith Shard~ Gleam is not, strictly speaking, a technique — it is the Berg defending itself, or remembering how to. It manifests as crystalline formations in geometric fractal patterns that resist direct observation, sharp enough to sever bone but more dangerous for what they carry: wounds inflicted by the shards bleed not the victim's blood alone but the Berg's frozen memories, drawn sideways through the temporal membrane.
    
    The shards do not always take crystalline form. Accounts describe organic manifestations — tooth, spine, bone-mineral composites — edged with the same impossible geometry. These can embed in living tissue, persisting as pressure and warmth long after the visible formation dissolves. The orca war-leader Grandfather Blood carried a permanent shard in his empty eye socket after an encounter in the deep, suggesting the phenomenon does not discriminate by species.
    
    ## Discovery and Known Sites
    
    Augur ☽'Milucaum~ Shadow-bane, the Nightshelf artificer and shadow-worker, claimed the ability during the Frozen Peace after encountering it at Scar☽ Sanctcaetiata, a geothermal vent in the Berg's deep ice that had never properly healed from the Orca Incursion. The phenomenon has since been documented at Wane☽ Oncea, the contested southern trade hub, and ☽'dwell Teneanemus~, the deep-carved ritual chamber beneath it.
    
    Three known manifestation sites along a single geothermal corridor. I note this without interpretation.
    
    ## Cost
    
    Each channeling bleeds the practitioner's own memories into the ice, leaving them progressively unmade. ☽'Milucaum~ demonstrated increasing hesitation in later accounts — sentences abandoned mid-thought, mourning without object, names dissolving. The Berg's ice gains what the practitioner loses. Whether this constitutes payment, theft, or simple thermodynamics of memory, the sources do not agree.
